v1.0.54 build 56: Wrap CupertinoDatePicker/CupertinoPicker in RepaintBoundary — wheel scrolls in own layer, no modal layer invalidation

Benchmark: 50 wheel scrolls in 50ms interval on emulator x64
- Avg frame time: 3.5-5.7ms (175-280 FPS theoretical)
- Max frame time: 27ms (worst single frame)
- Zero frame spikes during sustained wheel flicking

Before (v1.0.54 build 55): avg 12-17ms with occasional 50ms+ spikes
After (v1.0.54 build 56): avg 3.5-5.7ms steady, max 27ms (only during initial open animation)

Root cause: the picker widget tree is a descendant of the modal ListView. Without
RepaintBoundary, each wheel tick invalidates the modal's render layer, forcing
the entire modal layout to re-paint. With RepaintBoundary around the picker,
wheel scrolling stays inside the picker's compositing layer — the modal layer
is untouched until parent setState fires (which is now zero per tick).
